::kind(writ)

=[ Writ: layers-bare fixture ]

==[ crate-layering ]

@rule(crate-layering)

The whole declaration, written without its `{...}`. This is a realistic
mistake -- the heading names a rule this tool implements, and the data it
needs is simply absent.

`@layers` on its own line is not parsed as an element, so the guard finds
no declaration and reports nothing. Nothing distinguishes that from a
workspace with no layering rule at all.
